[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528218606","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112682#issuecomment-3528218606","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112682","id":3528218606,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7STFfu","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T15:02:23Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T15:24:10Z","body":"In my latest push, I've:\r\n\r\n- Renamed the flag from `CONNECT_UNIQUE_BIND` to `CONNECT_UNIQUE` based on @Mickeon's suggestion\r\n- Added a checkbox for the flag to the connection dialog in the editor. For new connections, it is checked by default! Since this only affects new connections, there shouldn't be compatibility issues, and I think this behavior is closer to user expectations, especially if the user adds extra call arguments in the dialog. But I'm fine to switch the default if there's push back on that\r\n- ~~Added an `is_connected_unique()` - there wasn't really a nice way to make `is_connected()` work automatically (like with `disconnect()`). I also tried adding an argument to `is_connected()` rather than adding a new method, but I didn't like the way the GDScript looked - it wasn't very clear what the `true` or `false` argument meant at a glance - so I switched to adding a new method~~\r\n- Updated the docs, including in `connect()`, `disconnect()` and `is_connected()` on both `Object` and `Signal`, to try and make the whole picture clearer\r\n\r\nSo, the only remaining thing on my TODO to take this out of DRAFT is to do a bunch more testing!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528218606/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528330393","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112682#issuecomment-3528330393","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112682","id":3528330393,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7STgyZ","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T15:23:44Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T15:23:44Z","body":"On chat, @Ivorforce pointed out that my rationale for adding `is_connected_unique()` was flawed! So, I've removed that now :-)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528330393/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536932517","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112682#issuecomment-3536932517","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112682","id":3536932517,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S0U6l","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-15T21:42:44Z","updated_at":"2025-11-15T21:42:44Z","body":"I've now done a bunch of testing (and fixed a small issue), so I'm taking this out of draft now","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536932517/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4366181947","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112682#issuecomment-4366181947","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112682","id":4366181947,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBD6mOw","user":{"login":"jinyangcruise","id":42859362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyODU5MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42859362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise","html_url":"https://github.com/jinyangcruise","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-03T12:35:31Z","updated_at":"2026-05-03T12:35:31Z","body":"How about naming it `CONNECT_ALLOW_SAME_CALLABLE` which allows users to connect a signal to the same callable multiple times, even the arguments are same.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4366181947/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4366372526","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112682#issuecomment-4366372526","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112682","id":4366372526,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBEGOrg","user":{"login":"jinyangcruise","id":42859362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyODU5MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42859362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise","html_url":"https://github.com/jinyangcruise","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-03T14:17:00Z","updated_at":"2026-05-03T14:17:00Z","body":"> How about naming it `CONNECT_ALLOW_SAME_CALLABLE` which allows users to connect a signal to the same callable multiple times, even the arguments are same.\r\n\r\nIt’s still a bit flawed in essence. What I actually want to say is that our  CONNECT_REFCOUNTED  implementation has some defects.\r\nWhen connecting multiple times, it only inserts the Callable from the first connection into the connection list. For subsequent connection calls, it merely increments the reference count, instead of pushing the new Callable (may have different bind args) into the connection list.\r\n \r\nThis causes a critical issue: even if you bind different parameters in later connections, the Callable that gets invoked is still the one registered on the first connection.\r\n \r\nIf we fix this defect in  CONNECT_REF COUNTED instead of creating new CONNECT_* flags, we can resolve many similar problems. What’s more, this change won’t break compatibility at all — it’s essentially just fixing an underlying bug, isn’t it?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4366372526/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]